[
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<p>Each section names a part of the media library, links to it on this service and lists steps to try it. The sample images are in the library already: the service puts them there with the pages under /development-testing. Sign in as the dev admin first (<a href=\"/dev/impersonate/admin\">sign in as the dev admin</a>).</p><p>The service puts these pages back as they were each time it starts. Edits to the pages are lost then, but changes to the sample images stay.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "The library, upload and image pages"
          },
          "anchor": "the-library-upload-and-image-pages"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/admin/media\">Media library</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0201\">The sample PNG</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0203\">The sample photo (JPEG)</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0204\">The sample animation (GIF)</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0202\">The sample SVG</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the media library. Search for “blocks”, then use the filters “Unused” and “Missing alt text”.</li><li>Drag two or more image files onto the upload area. Each file shows its progress, then a link to its image page.</li><li>Open the sample PNG. Change its alt text, caption, credit and tags, then save. Check the audit log for the change.</li><li>Under “Where the image is used”, check that the Image test page and the Media rich text test page are listed.</li><li>Under “Replace the image”, choose another file and select “Upload new version”. The image page shows version 2, and the Image test page shows the new file.</li><li>Duplicate check: save <a href=\"/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0201/1/blocks.png\">the sample PNG’s file</a>, then upload it again. The library says the image is already there and links to it.</li><li>The library uses the full width of the screen. On a wide screen the grid shows more than three images in a row.</li><li>Above the images, choose “Details” in the View list. The page changes at once, and the address has view=details. Each image is a table row: a small thumbnail, the name, and its type, dimensions, file size, alt text, uses and who uploaded it, and when.</li><li>Choose “Large”. Each image is on its own row, at a large size, with the same facts.</li><li>Search, tick a filter, select Apply, or go to page 2. The view stays. “Clear search and filters” keeps it too.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "The Image widget, crop and focal point"
          },
          "anchor": "the-image-widget-crop-and-focal-point"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/development-testing/widgets/image-test-page\">Image test page</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/pages/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0110/edit\">Edit the Image test page</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the Image test page. Each image comes from the library, at the width and crop the widget sets.</li><li>Edit the page. Open an Image widget and select “Choose image” to open the picker. Search, choose and upload from the picker.</li><li>Select “Crop image”. Try each crop shape, then drag the crop box. Type a crop to see the crop box follow it.</li><li>Select “Set focal point” and click the part to keep, or use the arrow keys.</li><li>Select “Crop image” and choose the 16:9 shape. “Set focal point” is now turned off, and a hint says why: the crop is already in that shape, so the focal point has no effect.</li><li>Choose the Free shape, or select “Reset crop”. “Set focal point” is turned on again.</li><li>Tick “This image is decorative”. The alt text clears, and the page writes an empty alt.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Rich text with library images"
          },
          "anchor": "rich-text-with-library-images"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/development-testing/media-rich-text-test-page\">Media rich text test page</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/pages/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0006/edit\">Edit the Media rich text test page</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the page. Each image is a library image with signed, resized copies.</li><li>Edit the page. In a rich text widget, select Insert/edit image, then the browse button, to choose from the library.</li><li>Paste an image into the editor. It uploads to the library, and the editor then uses the library file.</li><li>In the image dialog, tick “Image is decorative”. The image gets an empty alt and role=\"presentation\", and the editor gives no alt text warning.</li><li>Remove the alt text from an image that is not decorative. The editor shows a warning.</li><li>Choose a library image in the image dialog. Select “Constrain proportions” to unlock it, then give the image another shape, for example a width of 400 and a height of 200. Save and publish. The page shows the image in that shape, also in a narrow window. The “An image stretched in the editor” section of the test page shows one.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
