        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/development-testing/embedded-image-test-page\">Embedded image test page</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/move-embedded\">Move embedded images</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the Embedded image test page. Its image is a data: image inside the page text.</li><li>Open Move embedded images. The dry run lists the page and the number of images it will move.</li><li>Select the “Move … images” button. The page now shows a library image, and the library has the new image.</li><li>Run the move again. It has nothing to do.</li><li>To put the data: image back, restart the service, or press “Seed sample CMS pages” under System administration.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "A content block with an image"
          },
          "anchor": "a-content-block-with-an-image"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/admin/content-blocks?edit=development-testing-image#edit-development-testing-image\">Edit the image content block</a></li><li><a href=\"/content-block/versions/development-testing-image\">The block’s version history</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0203\">The sample photo’s image page</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the block’s version history. The current version shows the sample photo.</li><li>Open the sample photo’s image page. Under “Used in these content blocks”, the block is listed.</li><li>Edit the block and add another library image with the image dialog. Save, then check the new image’s image page.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Alt text and size reports"
          },
          "anchor": "alt-text-and-size-reports"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/admin/media/reports/alt-text\">Alt text report</a></li><li><a href=\"/admin/media/reports/size\">Size report</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the alt text report. The sample animation has no alt text, and the Media rich text test page uses the photo with the weak alt text “photo”.</li><li>The decorative image on the Media rich text test page is not listed.</li><li>Open the size report. It shows the totals, the space the resized copies use and the largest images.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Content staging export and import"
          },
          "anchor": "content-staging-export-and-import"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/admin/content-staging\">Content staging</a></li></ul><ol><li>Export the /development-testing pages. The bundle holds mediaAssets and mediaFiles for every image the pages and blocks use.</li><li>Import the same bundle. The result says “Images: … already here”.</li><li>Import it on another stack. The images arrive with the same ids, and the pages show them.</li><li>The bundle wins. Change the alt text of a sample image in the library, then import the bundle again. The result says “1 updated”, and the image has the bundle’s alt text again.</li><li>Import never deletes an image. Use “Delete unused images” for that.</li></ol>"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Delete unused images"
          },
          "anchor": "delete-unused-images"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/admin/media?unused=true\">Media library, unused images only</a></li></ul><ol><li>Upload two images with the same new word in their names, for example test-unused.</li><li>Open the library. Tick “Not used on any page”, search for the word, and select Apply.</li><li>Select “Delete unused images”. The confirmation page lists only the unused images that match the search.</li><li>Select “Delete 2 images”. The library says how many it deleted. The audit log has a “Unused images deleted from the media library” row.</li><li>The sample images are used by these pages, so they are never listed.</li></ol>"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "The picker needs the Media section"
          },
          "anchor": "the-picker-needs-the-media-section"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<ul><li><a href=\"/admin/system/roles\">Role settings</a></li></ul><ol><li>As the dev admin, untick Media for the editor role (cypmd_content_access_user) and save.</li><li>Sign in as the dev editor (open /dev/impersonate/editor) and edit the Image test page. The Image widget has no “Choose image” button, only the Image ID field. The rich text editor takes no pasted images.</li><li>Type the id of a sample image into the Image ID field and save. The widget shows it.</li><li>Sign in as the dev admin again, tick Media for the editor role and save.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "SVG sanitising"
          },
          "anchor": "svg-sanitising"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<p>Save this text as hostile.svg, then upload it to the library. The upload is accepted, and the stored file has no script, event handler, javascript: link, external address, @import or foreignObject. Open the stored file to see what is left.</p><pre><code>&lt;svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" viewBox=\"0 0 120 60\" onload=\"alert('onload')\"&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;@import url(https://example.com/x.css); rect { stroke: url(https://example.com/p.svg#a); }&lt;/style&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;alert('script')&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;rect width=\"120\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#d4351c\"/&gt;\n  &lt;a xlink:href=\"javascript:alert('link')\"&gt;&lt;text x=\"10\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#ffffff\"&gt;Hostile sample&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;image href=\"https://example.com/tracker.png\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"/&gt;\n  &lt;foreignObject width=\"10\" height=\"10\"&gt;&lt;div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"&gt;x&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/foreignObject&gt;\n&lt;/svg&gt;</code></pre><p>Save this text as entity.svg, then upload it. The library refuses it, because it has a DTD.</p><pre><code>&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\"?&gt;\n&lt;!DOCTYPE svg [&lt;!ENTITY word \"entity\"&gt;]&gt;\n&lt;svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"&gt;&lt;text&gt;&amp;word;&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;</code></pre><p>The library serves an SVG with its own content security policy. Open the developer tools, then open <a href=\"/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0202/1/blocks.svg\">the sample SVG’s file</a> and look at its Content-Security-Policy header.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "kind": "region",
    "layout": "single",
    "columns": [
      [
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Signed resized copies"
          },
          "anchor": "signed-resized-copies"
        },
        {
          "kind": "widget",
          "type": "richtext",
          "props": {
            "html": "<p>A resized or cropped copy must carry the signature the server adds to its address. A changed or missing signature, or a width outside the fixed set, gets an error.</p><ul><li><a href=\"/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0201/1/blocks.png\">The original file (works)</a></li><li><a href=\"/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0201/1/blocks.webp?w=640\">A copy 640 pixels wide, with no signature (error 400)</a></li><li><a href=\"/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0201/1/blocks.webp?w=640&amp;sig=tampered\">A copy with a changed signature (error 400)</a></li><li><a href=\"/media/00000000-cd94-4a01-8f01-0000000e0201/1/blocks.webp?w=500&amp;sig=tampered\">A width outside the fixed set (error 400)</a></li></ul><ol><li>Open the Image test page and look at the page source. Each src and srcset address has w= and sig=.</li><li>Open one of those addresses. Then change one letter of its sig= value. The changed address gets error 400.</li><li>Open the links above. Only the original file works.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      ]
    ]
  }
]

